From 93e9a44e67689be783d13becc93cffd7ba39cf43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:42:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a park awaiting a card on another gateway
 re-probes when that card's status change reaches the replica

A park on `hermes kanban wait-check task <id>` or awaiting={kind: card, ref: <id>} was re-probed only every
check_every (default 900 s), so PR #2277's owner slept ~10 min after its exact-head review approved on worker-1,
holding the land lane (t_01a1d57d2d295afd). The replica pull now reports its applied status changes
(ApplyResult/Pulled.status_changed); the sync round hands them to kanban_awaited_card_wake.expedite, which makes
the probe of every scheduled park naming a changed card due now and wakes the dispatcher. The probe stays the
judge (--from/--until unchanged; an unmet change costs one probe), no periodic polling is added, and the
wake-check tick logs one awaited_card_done_park_lag WARNING for a park still asleep 2 min after its awaited card
finished.
